  "locked": false,
  "title": "Don't set force async to false in Fragment scripting mode",
  "user": {
    "login": "noamr",
    "id": 88566,
    "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjg4NTY2",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88566?v=4",
    "gravatar_id": "",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/noamr",
    "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/followers",
    "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/following{/other_user}",
    "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/gists{/gist_id}",
    "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "In the `Fragment` scripting mode (used by `createContextualFragment()`, `setHTMLUnsafe()` and the positional `*HTMLUnsafe()` methods with `runScripts: true`, and `innerHTML`/`outerHTML`/`insertAdjacentHTML()` when a Trusted Types default policy enables `runScripts`), the HTML parser does not set the `script` element's `parser document`. Previously, it still set `force async` to false, and because `prepare the script element` only resets `force async` to true when `parser document` is non-null, external scripts without `async` kept `force async` set to false once inserted.\n\nAll three browser engines (Chromium, Gecko, and WebKit) instead leave `force async` as true in this case (`script.async` returns `true` before insertion, and external scripts without `async` execute as async once inserted).\n\nOnly set `force async` to false in `#scriptTag` when `scripting mode` is not `Fragment` (i.e., when `parser document` is set).\n\nFixes #13079.\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium (already matches this behavior)\n   * Gecko (already matches this behavior)\n   * WebKit (already matches this behavior)\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/63708\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: N/A (already implemented)\n   * Gecko: N/A (already implemented)\n   * WebKit: N/A (already implemented)\n- [x] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: N/A\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: N/A\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n#scriptTag\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13080/parsing.html#scriptTag\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 16, 2026, 3:28 PM UTC (9b897a3)\">/parsing.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13080/790ce89...9b897a3/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 16, 2026, 3:28 PM UTC (9b897a3)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13080/scripting.html#scriptTag\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 16, 2026, 3:28 PM UTC (9b897a3)\">/scripting.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13080/790ce89...9b897a3/scripting.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 16, 2026, 3:28 PM UTC (9b897a3)\">diff</a> )",
